    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0907" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg693"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 315.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Torbert to Mr.
                        Fish</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 48.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 21, 1871</date>. (Received May 16.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The undersigned, minister resident, has the
                    honor to inclose herewith a copy, and translation of the same, (marked A,) of a
                    dispatch received from the minister of foreign relations for Salvador and his
                    answer to the same, (marked B.)</p>
                <p>This has been a delicate and painful duty for me; so the first note which was
                    received I showed to Señor Dueñas, and he not being satisfied with the wording
                    as to the guarantee of his life, I requested the minister to send another with
                    more explicit language, which he did; and the note inclosed was approved by
                    Señor Dueñas, who is a lawyer by profession and is willing to be tried by the
                    laws of his country.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALFRED T. A. TORBERT.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d336-a1.xml" xpointer="d336-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d336-a2.xml" xpointer="d336-a2"/>
